# Mutation plan for the five team-administration routes.
#
#   scripts/mutate-batch.sh scripts/mutations/team-admin.plan
#
# The twin of `channel-admin.plan`, and the anchors are longer than that plan's were because the
# two `…MembersMinusGroupMembers` queries now sit in one file: `ORDER BY u.username ASC`,
# `LIMIT $3 OFFSET $4` and `count(DISTINCT u.id)` each occur twice, so every line here carries the
# `tm.`/`teammembers` alias that names the team query alone.
#
# What is worth mutating on each route:
#
#   * the page query's five predicates — `TeamMembers.DeleteAt` is the one with no channel
#     counterpart, and its fixture row is planted by SQL because no route writes it;
#   * `count(DISTINCT Users.Id)` against the page query's `GROUP BY`;
#   * `scheme`'s `|| id.is_empty()`, which is the whole difference from the channel handler, and
#     its **501** against the channel handler's 403;
#   * `invite/email`'s two permission checks, both of which report `invite_user`, and the three
#     400s in front of the hand-over;
#   * `import`'s seven refusals, and the two branches that decide whether a request is forwarded
#     at all — a mutation that forwards too much is how this route would start writing.
#
# **`invite-reports-add-user-to-team` is expected to SURVIVE, and it is not a fixture gap.** The
# permission a 403 *names* reaches only `detailed_error`, which `WipeDetailed` blanks on both
# servers whenever `EnableDeveloper` is false — the default, and not ported. The two bodies are
# byte-identical, so no HTTP test can see it; the line stays as the record that it was asked.
# `parity::team_admin::invite_asks_for_add_user_to_team_as_well_as_invite_user` asserts the
# `detailed_error` is empty on both, which is the observable half.
#
# The last two lines are the no-op controls and must SURVIVE.
team-page-keeps-team-members-removed-from-the-team	crates/mm-store/src/group_store.rs	             WHERE tm.deleteat = 0\n               AND t.deleteat = 0\n               AND u.deleteat = 0\n               AND b.userid IS NULL\n               AND t.id = $1\n               AND u.id NOT IN (\n                     SELECT igm.userid\n                       FROM groupmembers igm\n                       JOIN usergroups iug ON iug.id = igm.groupid\n                      WHERE igm.deleteat = 0\n                        AND igm.groupid = ANY($2)\n                   )\n             GROUP BY u.id, tm.schemeguest, tm.schemeadmin, tm.schemeuser\n	             WHERE (tm.deleteat = 0 OR TRUE)\n               AND t.deleteat = 0\n               AND u.deleteat = 0\n               AND b.userid IS NULL\n               AND t.id = $1\n               AND u.id NOT IN (\n                     SELECT igm.userid\n                       FROM groupmembers igm\n                       JOIN usergroups iug ON iug.id = igm.groupid\n                      WHERE igm.deleteat = 0\n                        AND igm.groupid = ANY($2)\n                   )\n             GROUP BY u.id, tm.schemeguest, tm.schemeadmin, tm.schemeuser\n	api	team_admin
